        "April brings the wheat and gram harvest across the district, when farm families are stretched and older children are needed at home. May and June bring heat that regularly passes forty degrees, and the monsoon arrives mainly in July and August. A shorter session with a break beats a long afternoon block when the fan is the only relief.",
        "The exam side of the year runs in parallel. Diploma students sit in May and get results in early July, with a November session for retakes. Cambridge IGCSE runs in May-June and October-November; Edexcel offers January, May-June and November. Madhya Pradesh Board and CBSE finals fall in February and March, so a child doing both has a crowded spring and benefits from planning in January.",
        "For a Diploma student the second half of Class 12 holds Internal Assessment deadlines, predicted grades for university applications and the May mocks. Starting in Class 11 gives room to meet them without panic.",
