        "Analysis and Approaches suits a student leaning towards engineering, physics or economics; Applications and Interpretation suits one more comfortable with data, modelling and technology. The choice is made in Class 11, and moving later is possible but costs weeks. Higher Level AA's third paper rewards a student who has met unfamiliar problems many times, not one who has read many solutions.",
        "The sciences have a Maihar-specific wrinkle, which is access to a well-equipped lab. A student studying online or alongside a CBSE school may not get IB-style practical sessions. The internal investigation can still be done well using simulations, open data sets and safe home experiments of the kind the IB permits, and a tutor helps design a question that suits the equipment available instead of one that needs a lab.",
        "Physics Higher Level asks for quick, confident data-booklet use and clean mechanics. Chemistry Higher Level turns on organic mechanisms and energetics once the first term's bonding and moles are secure. Biology turns on command terms and on statistics that stand up in the investigation. Students from CBSE or the Madhya Pradesh Board usually know the content well and under-practise the exact wording of IB questions.",
