  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find IB and IGCSE tutors in Maihar?", answer: "Send IB Gram your child's programme or board, subject, level and exam session, and we shortlist tutors who have taught that exact course. Because no Maihar school teaches the IB or IGCSE, matching is done on syllabus fit, not on location. A free trial lesson follows, at a time that suits your household, before any commitment is made." },
    { question: "Do tutors come to our home in Maihar?", answer: "No. In-person home tuition runs only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, so every lesson in Maihar is a live online session between one tutor and one student. The home part is where your child sits: private tuition from your own study table, with a laptop and shared whiteboard doing the work a visiting tutor's notebook would do." },
    { question: "Can my child study the IB or IGCSE if no school in Maihar offers it?", answer: "Yes, through an online or distance school, a boarding school elsewhere, or by following the syllabus with a tutor beside the present school. Which route fits depends on whether you need a formal certificate or readiness for a future move. We explain the options plainly and never push a relocation that the family does not need." },
    { question: "What does IB or IGCSE tuition cost in Maihar?", answer: "It depends on the programme and level, session length, weekly hours and how scarce the right specialist is, and we confirm your figure in writing before the trial. Higher Level Diploma subjects usually cost more than IGCSE Core or MYP work. Online lessons carry no travel cost, there is no long contract, and you can pause or stop without penalty." },
    { question: "Which schools near Maihar teach the IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None in Maihar itself could be confirmed. The nearest we can name are Little World School in Tilwara, Jabalpur, listed for IGCSE beside CBSE, and Eastern Public School and The Sanskaar Valley School in Bhopal, both listed for IGCSE, with Eastern Public School also listed for IB. Please confirm any school's current offer on its own admissions page." },
    { question: "Will online lessons work with our internet and power cuts?", answer: "Usually yes, if the plan allows for the occasional drop. Keep a charged laptop, a phone hotspot as backup and a quiet corner, and the tutor will save the whiteboard so a broken session can resume. We test the connection in the free trial lesson and agree a fallback, such as finishing on audio, before regular lessons begin." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson before we commit?", answer: "Yes. Every match begins with a free trial lesson in which your child works through a real topic from their syllabus with the tutor, online and with no obligation. Afterwards the tutor suggests a first-month plan and you decide whether to continue, ask for changes or try someone else." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with an Internal Assessment or the Extended Essay?", answer: "Yes, but only as a coach. A tutor can help choose a workable question, explain what each criterion rewards, plan data collection and give honest feedback on drafts. Writing or rewriting any part of assessed work breaks the IB's academic integrity rules, and our tutors decline such requests whatever the pressure." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you cover for Maihar students?", answer: "The usual DP choices: Maths Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science, Psychology and Hindi, at Higher or Standard Level, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay coaching. If your subject is unusual, ask and we will say honestly whether we have a suitable tutor." },
    { question: "Do you teach IB MYP and PYP, or only the Diploma?", answer: "We teach across the continuum. MYP help from Maihar usually means criterion-based writing in sciences, language and individuals and societies, plus the Personal Project process. PYP help covers reading, writing, number sense and Exhibition research habits, in short lessons that suit a younger child's attention span." },
    { question: "My child studies under the Madhya Pradesh Board or CBSE and wants to move to IB or IGCSE. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes, and it is one of our commonest Maihar requests. The gap is usually question style, not content: command words, structured explanation and independent project work need explicit teaching. A tutor works through your child's current school topics and rebuilds them in the style the new course expects." },
    { question: "When should we start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Ideally at the start of the course, Class 11 for the Diploma and Grade 9 for IGCSE, which leaves time to fix foundations before internal exams and predicted grades arrive. A later start still helps, with lessons aimed at the highest-value topics and past papers ahead of the exam series." },
    { question: "Can lessons be planned around Navratri, harvest and exams?", answer: "Yes, scheduling is one of the main advantages of online tuition. We fix a weekly slot after school, move or pause lessons during Navratri week, lighten the load in the April harvest rush if the family needs it, and add extra sessions ahead of mocks and board exams." },
    { question: "Should my child take Cambridge IGCSE or Edexcel IGCSE?", answer: "Usually the choice is made by the school or online provider, not by the tutor. Cambridge is the more common board in India, while Edexcel offers a January session and different paper styles. If you do have a choice, we compare the specifications for your child's subjects and strengths, and then match a tutor who knows that board." },
    { question: "Will an IB or IGCSE qualification be accepted by Indian colleges?", answer: "Generally yes, with paperwork. Indian universities usually ask for an equivalence certificate from the Association of Indian Universities, and entrance exams such as JEE, NEET and CUET set their own subject rules. Check each exam's current bulletin early, ideally before subject choices are locked in Class 11." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor?", answer: "Tell us and we will find someone else. Progress is reviewed with you every few weeks, and a change of tutor is routine, not a complaint. There is no long contract, so pausing or stopping lessons carries no penalty." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any Maihar school, the IB, Cambridge or Pearson?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no affiliation to or endorsement from any school in Maihar, the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. School names on this page only describe the local landscape and the nearest campuses." },
    { question: "We may be transferred out of Maihar mid-year. Can lessons continue?", answer: "Yes, and this is where online tutoring is strongest. The same tutor teaches at the same time from your new city, so a child keeps the syllabus and the relationship through a posting. We can also advise on matching the new school's board and exam session." },
  ],

